#6319
The Tomb of the Abbess~
   A round vault with a marble sarcophagus at its centre, its lid cast aside
and cracked in two. The walls are scored with spirals scratched into the
stone by fingernails. The Abbess who founded the hospice rose first, and the
others rose because she called them.
